From e721359e5ad0292d93bb9779c4b09fbeb681c266 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haoxiang Li <haoxiang_li2024@163.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:20:12 +0800
Subject: KVM: PPC: Book3S HV: Clean up on uvmem initialization failure

References: bsc#1215199
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc4
Git-commit: e721359e5ad0292d93bb9779c4b09fbeb681c266

When kvmppc_uvmem_init() fails, kvmppc_book3s_init_hv() returns
directly, bypassing the existing error path. Jump to the existing
error path to clean up before returning the error.

Fixes: 175be7e5800e ("KVM: PPC: Book3S HV: Free allocated memory if module init fails")
Signed-off-by: Haoxiang Li <haoxiang_li2024@163.com>
Reviewed-by: Fabiano Rosas <farosas@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Ritesh Harjani (IBM) <ritesh.list@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Madhavan Srinivasan <maddy@linux.ibm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261118102012.2252221-1-haoxiang_li2024@163.com
Acked-by: Michal Suchanek <msuchanek@suse.de>
---
 arch/powerpc/kvm/book3s_hv.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/powerpc/kvm/book3s_hv.c b/arch/powerpc/kvm/book3s_hv.c
index bafe9546087b..4f45b1b33561 100644
--- a/arch/powerpc/kvm/book3s_hv.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/kvm/book3s_hv.c
@@ -6745,7 +6745,7 @@ static int kvmppc_book3s_init_hv(void)
 	r = kvmppc_uvmem_init();
 	if (r < 0) {
 		pr_err("KVM-HV: kvmppc_uvmem_init failed %d\n", r);
-		return r;
+		goto err;
 	}
 
 #if defined(CONFIG_KVM_XICS)
